  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Equal opportunities for greater diversity in Adjara</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The activity is about creating employment opportunities for Muslim women and queer individuals/activists living in Adjara. This issue is tackled from two sides: by enhancing these groups&apos; mental health/well-being, and by offering them practical and professional skills to help find work.

Objectives:
1. Enhance mental health and professional skills for Muslim women;
2. Support queer community in Adjara via mental and physical health services and career development opportunities;
3.	Familiarize Adjarian Muslim women and queer community with the labour market in the region.

Activities:
- A 5-day workshop for 20 Muslim women from Adjara (mental health, professional skills); 
- A 4-day workshop for 25 queers from Adjara (well-being, professional skills); 
- Four thematic meetings (two for Muslim women and two for queers) on the topics of the participants&apos; interest; 
- Funding 35 participants to follow courses of their choice.
- Networking meeting do advocate participants&apos; employability.</narrative>
  </description>
